  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "Clothes shopping",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "The future for 'I' ends in **-ব** (*-bo*): **কিনব** 'I will buy'. For আপনি it's **-বেন**: **কিনবেন**. Put **না** after the verb: **কিনব না** 'I won't buy'. (You'll also see কিনবো.)\n\nClothes: **শাড়ি** (sari), **জামা** (shirt / top / dress), **লুঙ্গি** (the wrap many men wear at home). **-টা** gives 'the': **শাড়িটা**, **জামাটা**. Colours go first: **লাল শাড়ি**. Careful: **শাড়ি** (*shari*) sounds close to **সাড়ে** (*share*).\n\n**কোনো … নেই** = 'no … at all': **কোনো সমস্যা নেই**.\n\n*Culture:* clothing markets are where bargaining is most expected.",
